            "review_title": "Review at Hai San Sam Son",
            "review_text": "patarapong\nBangkok, Thailand151 contributions\n0\na strange but warm experience at this restaurant.\nNov 2014 • Family\nwe brought our own wine to this restaurant,at first a waiter told us that there was some corkage fee which we agreed. then came a kind waitress to take order,she said it was free for us. we ordered grouper lau which she said the grouper weigh 1.5 kg,and 3 other dishes. when i open my mouth to order the 5th dish she said something in vietnamese that showed we must stop ordering,she will not any further order.(a group of 4 adults). after enjoying dinner for a while we decide to order some more noodle and vegetable dishes. then she came and try to tell us that the lau already consists of noodle and a lot of vegetables. i've never dine in a restaurant like this before, she was a hard to find waitress,very kind and helpful with smiling face though she did not speak or understand much english. about the services,it was good,nothing to complain. the food taste very good. sea foods are very fresh. most of all the price is very reasonable.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 27, 2014",
